@startuml
title Post-run Experiment Evaluation and Dataset Comparison

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 12
skinparam ArrowColor #475569
skinparam activity {
  BackgroundColor #F8FAFC
  BorderColor #64748B
  FontColor #0F172A
  DiamondBackgroundColor #FEF3C7
  DiamondBorderColor #D97706
}
skinparam swimlane {
  BorderColor #CBD5E1
  TitleBackgroundColor #E2E8F0
  TitleFontColor #0F172A
}

|Admin / Researcher|
start
note right
  Entry point: Run Experiment confirmed.
  Steps 1-10 apply to each RAG or
  Fine-tuned experiment.
end note

|Evaluation Platform|
:1. Validate experiment, dataset, documents,\nquestions, and model; show any blocker;
:2. Freeze the dataset checksum\nand benchmark profile;
:3. Clear previous results, set QUEUED,\nthen start the selected experiment;
:4. Load benchmark questions in batches with\nground truth and expected source/page;

|AI Runtime / Evaluator|
:5. Generate answers:\nRAG retrieves frozen contexts;\nFine-tuned generates without retrieval;
:6. Build evaluation evidence from question,\nanswer, ground truth, contexts, and citations;
:7. Run Official RAGAS:\nanswer relevance plus RAG grounding metrics;
:8. Calculate token-overlap proxy,\nsource/page hit, refusal, and runtime metrics;

note right
  Official RAGAS:
  - Faithfulness
  - Answer relevance
  - Context precision / recall

  Internal:
  - Token-overlap proxy
  - Source / page hit
  - Refusal correctness
  - Latency / throughput
end note

|Evaluation Platform|
:9. Persist one result row per question\nand update success, failure, and progress;
:10. Finish the experiment as COMPLETED,\nFAILED, or CANCELLED;

|Admin / Researcher|
:11. Select one completed RAG run and\none completed Fine-tuned run;

|Evaluation Platform|
:12. Verify both runs use the same dataset,\nchecksum, and benchmark profile;
:13. Aggregate run averages, hit/success rates,\nlatency, and per-question deltas;

|Admin / Researcher|
:14. Review summary, question-level evidence,\nerrors and limits, then draw a conclusion;
stop

@enduml
